From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Eggleston <eggnet@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:36:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Don't keep the reply pipe's write end open during
 thread init.

init_thread_pipe() sends the write end of a new thread's reply pipe to
the server. Since 44699c324f2 the thread closes its own copy only after
its init_thread or init_first_thread request has returned.

If the thread is killed after it has written that request but before
the server has read it, the server closes the thread's request pipe and
the reply fd it was sent, and never replies. The thread keeps waiting
for the reply, and since it holds the write end itself, the read never
sees end-of-file: the thread stays blocked for the life of the process,
with its pipes and its stacks. A thread killed just before it writes
the request gets EPIPE and exits, but leaks the write end.

Close the write end as soon as the server has it, as before 44699c324f2.
The fd number is still what the request passes: the server looks it up
among the fds this thread has sent.

Helldivers 2's anti-tamper code creates suspended threads and kills them
right away, several times a second, so these threads pile up during a
session.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
index 8a02609bee1..0336bebc57f 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/server.c
@@ -1623,6 +1623,10 @@ static int init_thread_pipe(void)
     wine_server_send_fd( reply_pipe[1] );
     wine_server_send_fd( ntdll_get_thread_data()->wait_fd[1] );
     ntdll_get_thread_data()->reply_fd = reply_pipe[0];
+    /* The server has its own copy now. If we kept ours until the init request
+     * returns, a thread killed before the server reads the request would wait
+     * for the reply forever. */
+    close( reply_pipe[1] );
     return reply_pipe[1];
 }
 
@@ -1780,7 +1784,6 @@ size_t server_init_process(void)
         }
     }
     SERVER_END_REQ;
-    close( reply_pipe );
 
     if (ret) server_protocol_error( "init_first_thread failed with status %x\n", ret );
 
@@ -1899,7 +1902,6 @@ void server_init_thread( void *entry_point, BOOL *suspend )
         *suspend = reply->suspend;
     }
     SERVER_END_REQ;
-    close( reply_pipe );
 }
 
 NTSTATUS WINAPI NtAllocateReserveObject( HANDLE *handle, const OBJECT_ATTRIBUTES *attr,
